==Overview==
{{Tabber
|Pros|
{{Overview
|'''General'''
* Easy to obtain and very cheap to buy.
* Good mobility.
* All moves are able to [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* All moves are multi-target.
* Most moves have low end-lag.

|'''[Z] Knock'''
* Practically no startup time.
* Decent cooldown.

|'''[X] Spring Snipe'''
* Can be used for mobility.
* Decent range.

|'''[C] Spring Cannon'''
* Can be used for extending combos.

|'''[V] Spring Emperor'''
* Can deal above average damage if used correctly, though it's hard to pull this off.
* Can be used as a combo ender.

|'''[F] Spring Leap'''
* Bounces really fast, which makes it ideal for running and dodging attacks.
* No end-lag.
}}

|Cons|
{{Overview
|'''General'''
* Low damage output.
* Low [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* All moves can be dodged with [[Instinct]].
* Small hitboxes on almost every move.

|'''[Z] Knock'''
* Bad range.
* A bit easy to avoid.

|'''[X] Spring Snipe'''
* Easy to avoid.

|'''[C] Spring Cannon'''
* Bad midair.
* Easy to avoid.
* Can be easily punished if missed.

|'''[V] Spring Emperor'''
* Very unreliable as the player is not guaranteed to hit more than once (especially on open areas) and sometimes the move will not hit at all.
* Terrible for starting/extending combos as it often leads to going off the planned trajectory.

|'''[F] Spring Leap'''
* Hard to control correctly.
* Only really effective in areas with objects to rebound.
}}
}}

==Trivia==
* Spring is used by [[Jeremy]].
* The {{Ability|F}} ability can reach an incredible top speed if the user keeps bouncing, but quickly loses said speed.

